-- Fuller refund, terms and privacy pages, like other Australian cake shops: change of mind, cancelling
-- (48 hours, custom cakes 7 days), faulty cakes (same day, with photos), delivery, storage, cookies,
-- overseas services and how long records are kept. A page the shop already edited in
-- Admin > Pages is left as it is (only the original text is replaced).
UPDATE `pages` SET `body` = '<p>We want you to love your cake. Because every cake is fresh food, made to order for you, this policy explains when we can offer a refund, a credit or a replacement, and what to do if something is not right.</p>\n<h2>Change of mind</h2>\n<p>Cakes are perishable and made especially for your order, so we do not offer refunds or exchanges for a change of mind, or if you choose the wrong cake, size or date.</p>\n<h2>Cancelling or changing an order</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>48 hours or more before pickup or delivery:</strong> call us on {store_phone} and we will change the date, time or cake, or cancel the order with a full refund.</li>\n<li><strong>Less than 48 hours before:</strong> your cake may already be in preparation. We will always try to move it to another day, but we may not be able to offer a refund.</li>\n<li>Changes are only confirmed once we have replied to you. A message or email sent outside our opening hours is read the next day we are open.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Custom cakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A custom cake is booked once your quote is accepted and the deposit is paid.</li>\n<li>Cancel <strong>7 days or more</strong> before the event and we refund your deposit, less anything we have already spent on special ingredients or decorations.</li>\n<li>Cancel <strong>less than 7 days</strong> before and the deposit cannot be refunded, as your cake has been planned and its decorations made or ordered.</li>\n<li>Design changes are welcome up to 7 days before. Later changes depend on what we can still do, and may change the price.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>If something is wrong with your order</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Please check your cake when you collect it or when it is delivered, before you leave the shop or sign for it.</li>\n<li>If the cake is not what you ordered, is damaged, or there is a problem with its quality, tell us <strong>on the same day, and within 24 hours at the latest</strong>. Call {store_phone} or email {store_email} with your order number and photos of the cake.</li>\n<li>Please keep the cake, or what is left of it, until we have spoken with you.</li>\n<li>When the problem is ours, we will offer a replacement, a store credit or a refund, whichever suits you.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What we cannot cover</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Damage after the cake has been handed over, for example while it is carried or driven, or when it is left out of the fridge or in the heat.</li>\n<li>Small differences from photos. Every cake is handmade, so colours, decorations and shapes may vary a little.</li>\n<li>Personal taste, when the cake was made as ordered.</li>\n<li>Orders not collected on the day. We keep them until closing time; after that they cannot be refunded.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Delivery</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Someone needs to be at the address to receive the cake at the time we agree. We call you if no one answers.</li>\n<li>If no one is there, we take the cake back to the shop. You can collect it the same day, or we can deliver again for another delivery fee.</li>\n<li>Please tell the driver straight away if the cake arrives damaged, and send us a photo.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How refunds are paid</h2>\n<p>Approved refunds go back to the way you paid. Card refunds usually appear within 5 to 10 business days, depending on your bank. PayID and bank transfer refunds are sent to your account, and cash payments are refunded in the shop.</p>\n<h2>Your rights</h2>\n<p>Our cakes come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law. Nothing in this policy limits those rights.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'refund-policy' AND MD5(`body`) = 'f1efd4e3619eeb265c71a33e1c27cf8c';
UPDATE `pages` SET `body` = '<p>These terms apply when you place an order with {store_name}, on this website, by phone or in the shop. By placing an order you agree to them.</p>\n<h2>Orders</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Please order at least {min_lead_hours} hours before your pickup or delivery time for cakes from our menu, and at least {custom_lead_days} days ahead for custom cakes.</li>\n<li>You receive an order number and a confirmation email after you order. Please check the date, time and the message for the cake.</li>\n<li>Card orders are confirmed when the payment goes through. PayID and bank transfer orders are confirmed once we have checked your payment.</li>\n<li>Orders you pay for in the shop or on a phone call are booked when you place them and paid before or at pickup.</li>\n<li>We will contact you if we cannot make your order as placed, for example if an ingredient is unavailable, and refund anything you have paid for it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Prices and payment</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All prices are in Australian dollars and include GST where it applies.</li>\n<li>The price shown at checkout, including any delivery fee, is the price you pay. Custom cakes are priced by quote.</li>\n<li>We accept the ways to pay shown at checkout. Card payments are processed securely by Stripe; we never see your full card number.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Pickup</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Please collect your order from {store_address} at the time you chose. If you need to change it, call {store_phone} as early as you can.</li>\n<li>Orders not collected on the day are kept until closing time.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Delivery</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>We deliver to the areas and on the days shown at checkout. The delivery fee is shown before you pay.</li>\n<li>Someone needs to be at the address to receive the cake. See our <a href=\"{url:refund-policy}\">Refund and Cancellation Policy</a> for what happens if no one is there.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Looking after your cake</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Carry the cake flat, for example on the floor of the car, not on a seat, and keep it out of the sun.</li>\n<li>Keep cream cakes, cheesecakes and mousse cakes in the fridge, and enjoy them within 2 to 3 days.</li>\n<li>Once the cake has been handed over, it is your responsibility to transport and store it correctly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our cakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every cake is handmade, so colours, decorations and shapes may differ slightly from the photos on our website.</li>\n<li>For custom cakes, we match your design as closely as we can. Characters and printed images may be adapted.</li>\n<li>Our products are made in a kitchen that handles common allergens. Please read our <a href=\"{url:allergens}\">allergen information</a> before ordering, and tell us about any allergy when you order.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Cancellations and refunds</h2>\n<p>Please see our <a href=\"{url:refund-policy}\">Refund and Cancellation Policy</a>.</p>\n<h2>Photos of your cake</h2>\n<p>We sometimes share photos of cakes we have made on our website and social media. We never show your name or personal details. Tell us when you order if you would rather we did not share a photo of your cake.</p>\n<h2>Your rights</h2>\n<p>Nothing in these terms limits your rights under the Australian Consumer Law. These terms are governed by the law of the Australian Capital Territory.</p>\n<h2>Contact</h2>\n<p>{store_name}, {store_address}. Phone {store_phone}, email {store_email}.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'terms' AND MD5(`body`) = 'd6d7ede954cd9baa65db7c955d310dcf';
UPDATE `pages` SET `body` = '<p>{store_name} (\"we\", \"us\") respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal information we collect when you use our website, place an order or contact us, and how we handle it in line with the Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).</p>\n<h2>Information we collect</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Contact details:</strong> your name, email address and phone number when you place an order, request a custom cake quote, send us a message or create an account.</li>\n<li><strong>Order details:</strong> the cakes you order, messages for your cake, pickup or delivery date and time, delivery address (if used) and any notes you add.</li>\n<li><strong>Payment information:</strong> card payments are processed by Stripe. We never see or store your full card number. If you pay by PayID or bank transfer, we keep the payment screenshot or receipt you upload.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos and messages you send us:</strong> reference images with a custom cake request, and the messages and emails you send us.</li>\n<li><strong>Account details:</strong> if you create an account, we store your details and a securely encrypted version of your password.</li>\n<li><strong>Website use:</strong> like most websites, our server records technical details such as your IP address and browser, to keep the site secure and working.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How we use your information</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>To prepare your order and have it ready at the time you chose, or deliver it.</li>\n<li>To contact you about your order, your custom cake quote or your enquiry. This includes emails about your order, a reminder the day before, and after pickup an invitation to review us, which you can ignore.</li>\n<li>To check payments and keep the records required for tax and accounting.</li>\n<li>To show your orders and messages when you log in to your account.</li>\n<li>To improve our website and our service.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We do not sell your personal information. We do not send marketing emails unless you ask us to, and you can ask us to stop at any time.</p>\n<h2>Who we share it with</h2>\n<p>We only share information with the services we need to run the shop: our payment provider (Stripe), our website host, our email provider and, if you choose delivery, the person delivering your cake. They may only use it to provide their service to us. We will also share information when the law requires it.</p>\n<h2>Information stored overseas</h2>\n<p>Some of these services, such as Stripe and Google, may store information outside Australia, including in the United States. We use well-known providers that protect personal information.</p>\n<h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>\n<p>Our website uses a small session cookie so your cart and login work while you browse. We may use Google Analytics to see how visitors use the website, for example which pages are popular. It uses cookies but does not tell us who you are. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. We do not use advertising cookies.</p>\n<h2>How long we keep it</h2>\n<p>We keep order and payment records for at least 5 years, as Australian tax law requires. Other information is kept only as long as we need it, and you can ask us to delete your account at any time.</p>\n<h2>Keeping your information safe</h2>\n<p>We store your information on secure servers and limit access to staff who need it. Payment screenshots and reference photos are kept in a private area that is not publicly accessible. No website can be completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information, and we will tell you if a serious data breach affects you.</p>\n<h2>Children</h2>\n<p>Our website is meant for adults placing orders. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 16.</p>\n<h2>Accessing or correcting your information</h2>\n<p>You can update your details from your account page, or contact us to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you. We reply within 30 days.</p>\n<h2>Questions or complaints</h2>\n<p>Please contact us on {store_phone} or {store_email}. We will reply within 30 days. If you are not happy with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at <a href=\"https://www.oaic.gov.au\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">oaic.gov.au</a> or on 1300 363 992.</p>\n<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>\n<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version is always on this page.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'privacy-policy' AND MD5(`body`) = '11de92788d81496680e60e1fa9c64506';
